  "content": {
    "sequence": [
      {
        "step": 1,
        "text": "A roster does not require a partner. It requires a named shift and a named person to cover it — a support web, not a marriage contract. The night still needs an owner and a schedule.",
        "type": "hook"
      },
      {
        "step": 2,
        "text": "Nobody owns the night, so the default becomes she owns all of it. Doing 100% of nights, every night, for weeks — with no partner shift to hand off to.",
        "type": "problem"
      },
      {
        "step": 3,
        "text": "Schedules a support-web roster — named shifts for family, friends, or paid help — so the mother's protected block is physically real. A sleep banker makes exhaustion visible and tradeable even without a partner.",
        "type": "insight"
      },
      {
        "step": 4,
        "text": "Nights with zero protected block become a protected block of 3+ hours on most nights. The support web covers named shifts instead of the mother owning every night alone.",
        "type": "cta"
      }
    ]
  },
